# CM folding and the strongest generic comparator

## Mechanism

A subtree whose entire live function depends on one row variable and one column variable can be collapsed to four truth values before a large ANF expansion. Typed signed-frame metadata allows a structural CM route; four scalar evaluations provide retabulation; packed two-support/cut evaluation provides a generic route. An outer AND can create many monomial-pair products that disappear after cancellation. Folding the small function first avoids forming those pairs.

That saving can be real without being exclusive to the CM representation. The four-arm benchmark tests direct ANF, shared CSE, generic two-support optimization and CM folding on the same generated sources. It gives the generic comparator equivalent local truth-function power rather than forbidding it from making the obvious optimization.

## Recorded evidence

There are10,500 supplied raw rows. Of these10,389 completed in all four arms and111 did not. The admitted population is3,750 S1 plus6,639 S2. CM and generic tie on final degree, final monomial count, multiplication count, output unique nodes, pair terms, peak monomials and serialized bytes in every admitted case. The independent recount agrees with the supplied audit. The generic arm records more folds in6,010 cases and CM more in none; fold counters themselves are not performance claims.

The corrected S2 source is crucial. The earlier generator did not achieve requested live support in all cases, so its55.161 percent figure is historical, not mixed into the corrected100 percent supported population. Support guards and requested sharing ratios describe the generator; actual whole-formula support must be measured, not inferred from a selected core subtree.

SC-A passes as a symbolic-work mechanism gate. The natural-workload gates and external AIG/XAG/PolyBoRi checks are not supplied as completed campaigns. Paper B's separate confirmatory protocol requires end-to-end time, memory, reuse and a frozen corpus. None is licensed by the seven-metric equality table or by a single-pass diagnostic timing ratio.

## Paper decision

Keep this result in B. It clarifies both the value and the limit of typed CM fusion. A separate optimization paper becomes warranted only after one of three genuinely substantive results: reproducible lower recognition/compilation cost than strong generic methods; a distinct provenance/reuse/memory advantage with matched outputs; or a broad natural-workload negative result establishing an important boundary. 'Generic cuts can also do it' is not a reason to abandon engineering the optimization; it is a reason to ask the right comparative question.
